- **Invertible Integers Modulo \( n \)**: An integer \( a \) is invertible modulo \( n \) if there exists an integer \( b \) such that \( ab \equiv 1 \mod n \). This is true if and only if \( \gcd(a, n) = 1 \).
- **Non-invertible Integers Modulo \( n \)**: These are integers \( a \) for which \( \gcd(a, n) \neq 1 \).

