\[
-10 \equiv 21 \pmod{31}
\]
So, \( 3^{-1} \equiv 21 \pmod{31} \).

#### Step 3.2: Find \( 5^{-1} \pmod{31} \)
Now we solve:
\[
5y \equiv 1 \pmod{31}
\]
Using the Extended Euclidean Algorithm:
\[
