2025-07-13 01:58:12 - INFO - ### Problem Statement
We need to find the sum of all nice numbers in the set \(\{ 2010, 2011, 2012, \dots, 2019 \}\). A positive integer \(n\) is defined as nice if there exists a positive integer \(m\) with exactly four positive divisors such that the sum of these four divisors equals \(n\).

### Approach
A positive integer \(m\) has exactly four positive divisors if it can be expressed in one of two forms:
1. \(m = p^3\) for some prime \(p\). The divisors in this case are \(1, p, p^2, p^3\).
2. \(m = p \cdot q\) for two distinct primes \(p\) and \(q\). The divisors here are \(1, p, q, p \cdot q\).

The sum of the divisors for each case is calculated as follows:
