\]

This norm can also be computed as the largest singular value of the matrix \( A \).

### Step 2: Singular Value Decomposition

To find the singular values of \( A \), we can use the Singular Value Decomposition (SVD). The singular values are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix \( A^T A \).

