We solve 

\[
\begin{pmatrix} 19 - (45 + 15\sqrt{3}) & 30 \\ -45 & -71 - (45 + 15\sqrt{3}) \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = 0.
\]

This simplifies to:

\[
\begin{pmatrix} -26 - 15\sqrt{3} & 30 \\ -45 & -116 - 15\sqrt{3} \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = 0.
\]

From the first row, we have:

\[
