🔄 开始测试问题: Joe was in charge of lights for a dance. The red light blinks every two seconds, the yellow light every three seconds, and the blue light every five seconds. If we include the very beginning and very end of the dance, how many times during a seven minute dance will all the lights come on at the same time? (Assume that all three lights blink simultaneously at the very beginning of the dance.)

2025-07-13 02:00:39 - INFO - ```python
def solve():
    # Define the blinking intervals for each light in seconds
    red_blink = 2
    yellow_blink = 3
    blue_blink = 5
    
    # Calculate the least common multiple (LCM) of the blinking intervals
    from math import gcd
    
    def lcm(a, b):
        return abs(a * b) // gcd(a, b)
    
    # Calculate LCM of all three blinking intervals
    lcm_red_yellow = lcm(red_blink, yellow_blink)
    lcm_all = lcm(lcm_red_yellow, blue_blink)
    
    # Total duration of the dance in seconds
    dance_duration = 7 * 60  # 7 minutes
    
    # Count how many times all lights blink together
    # Including the very beginning and very end of the dance
    count = dance_duration // lcm_all + 1
    
    return count

# Call the solve function and print the result
result = solve()
print(result)
```
