### Step 2: Outline the Approach
Let \( x \) be the average score of the 6 tests Heidi has taken. The total score from these tests can be expressed as \( 6x \). The final exam counts as two tests, so if she scores 99 points, the total score from the final exam will be \( 99 \times 2 = 198 \).

