### Approach
To solve this problem, we can visualize the selection of the two numbers \( x \) and \( y \) as points in a unit square on the Cartesian plane, where \( x \) is on the horizontal axis and \( y \) is on the vertical axis. The area of this square is \( 1 \times 1 = 1 \).

