\]

Now we reduce \( 26103 \) modulo \( 508 \):

\[
26103 \div 508 \approx 51.4 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 51 \text{ (integer part)}
\]
\[
51 \cdot 508 = 25908
\]
\[
26103 - 25908 = 195
\]

Thus, we have:

\[
11^{-1} \equiv 195 \pmod{508}
\]

